    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 15.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.3" corresp="#wit-g-a">And se ðe on Dena lage riht lage wyrde, gylde he lahslit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.3" corresp="#wit-a">And se ðe on Dane laga rihte lage wyrde, gilde he lahslite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.3" corresp="#wit-d-frags">And se ðe Dene laga rihte laga wirde, gilde he lahslihte . . . .</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.3" corresp="#wit-q">In Denalaga lahslite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="15a.3" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ se ðe on Dena lage rihte lage wyrde, gylde hé lahslíte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And se ðe on Dena lage rihte lage wyrde, gylde he lahslit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And he who violates justice in the Danelaw shall pay <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And in the Danelaw, anyone who rejects just law is to pay lahslit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And he who violates just law in the Danelaw is to pay lahslit….</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wer im Dänen-Rechtsgebiet richtige Satzung (-gen D?) bricht, der zahle Rechtsbruchbusse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever in the Danelaw violates just law (laws, D?), let him pay lahslit.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_42-2">Leis Wl 42.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="464"><label>inserts</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_2">III Eg 2</ref> <quote>Here the code inserts III Edgar, 2, 4, 5–5.2, with unimportant variations.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="464"><label>inserts</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_4">III Eg 4</ref> <quote>Here the code inserts III Edgar, 2, 4, 5–5.2, with unimportant variations.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="464"><label>inserts</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5–5.2</ref> <quote>Here the code inserts III Edgar, 2, 4, 5–5.2, with unimportant variations.</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">In D, VI Atr 42 follows.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">Here the code inserts III Edgar, 2, 4, 5–5.2, with unimportant variations.</note>
      </div>
